<title>BELGIUM: EU ministers will discuss pig storage aid.</title>
<headline>EU ministers will discuss pig storage aid.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers will consider at Monday's Council whether to introduce private storage aid for pig meat blocked from being exported to Japan, an EU diplomat said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Denmark has asked for the item to be raised under any other business and it has a chance of support,&quot; the diplomat said.</p>
<p>The Danish government want private storage aid funded by the EU in order to store pig meat which is currently barred from the Japanese market.</p>
<p>Japan's right to block imports from its domestic market under GATT rules because average limits over the past three years were exceeded expires in July.</p>
<p>Denmark argues that aid is needed to store meat pending the reopening of the export trade.</p>
<p>&quot;This is certainly a more useful use of private storage aid than simply to remove surplus production from the EU market,&quot; the diplomat commented.</p>
<p>The decision to introduce aid is for the European Commission which will note the views of the Council on Monday, he added.</p>
</text>
